# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

A tool package for [Quant-Agent-OS](https://github.com/yuxuzi/quant-agent-os). Each tool is a
typed Python function. The platform runs it with input and output validation, permissions, a
timeout, and a recorded run, through MCP or the Python SDK.

## Develop

```bash
uv sync
uv run pytest                    # includes the platform's contract checks
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check .
uv run mypy {{ package_name }} tests
```

## Use the tools

```python
from quant_agent_os.sdk import Platform

from {{ package_name }} import registry

with Platform(registry()) as platform:
    record = platform.call("{{ tool_name }}", text="momentum and reversal")
    print(record.status, record.output)
```

Serve them to an MCP client such as Claude (needs `quant-agent-os[mcp]`):

```python
from quant_agent_os.mcp import run_stdio
from quant_agent_os.runtime import ToolExecutor
from quant_agent_os.tools import PermissionPolicy

from {{ package_name }} import registry

run_stdio(ToolExecutor(registry(), PermissionPolicy()), name="{{ project_name }}")
```

## Add a tool

Write a function that takes one pydantic model and returns another, decorate it with `@tool`,
add it to `tools()` in `{{ package_name }}/tools.py`, and add a `check_tool` test. Declare a
`Permission` for anything beyond reading its input.

